# DevIndex working set — every file the pipeline writes, which is all of them.
#
# The split was once "derived vs curated", chosen by which files were big enough to bloat git. Wrong
# axis. The right one is who WRITES it, and by that test the whole directory is pipeline state:
# `Cleanup` rewrites `allowlist`, `updateUsers` rewrites `threshold`, OptIn/OptOut advance their sync
# cursors, and **`OptOut` appends to `blocklist`** when someone asks to be removed.
#
# Keeping `blocklist.json` in git looked like protecting an audit trail and was the opposite: written
# in a runner and never published, an opt-out does not survive the run that honoured it — while the
# closing comment has already promised the user they were removed. History settles the intent too:
# one creation commit each in 2023, never edited since. The opt-in/opt-out ISSUE FLOW is the human
# interface, not the file.
/apps/devindex/resources/data/

